ious applications, friendly or otherwise, usually literal); ","kjv_def":"--assault, come (in, to, unto, upon), be at hand (instant), present, stand (before, by, over)","n":21,"o":"LUK2:9 LUK2:38 LUK4:39 LUK10:40 LUK20:1 LUK21:34 LUK24:4 ACT4:1 ACT6:12 ACT10:17 ACT11:11 ACT12:7 ACT17:5 ACT22:13 ACT22:20 ACT23:11 ACT23:27 ACT28:2 1TH5:3 2TI4:2 2TI4:6"},"G2187":{"lemma":"Ἐφραίμ","translit":"Ephraím","derivation":"of Hebrew origin (H0669 or better H06085);","strongs_def":" Ephraim, a place in Palestine","kjv_def":"Ephraim","n":1,"o":"JHN11:54"},"G2121":{"lemma":"εὔκαιρος","translit":"eúkairos","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G2540 (καιρός);","strongs_def":" well-timed, i.e. opportune","kjv_def":"convenient, in time of need","n":2,"o":"MRK6:21 HEB4:16"},"G2126":{"lemma":"εὐλαβής","translit":"eulabḗs","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G2983 (λαμβάνω);","strongs_def":" taking well (carefully), i.e. circumspect (religiously, pious)","kjv_def":"devout","n":3,"o":"LUK2:25 ACT2:5 ACT8:2"},"G2182":{"lemma":"ἐφευρετής","translit":"epheuretḗs","derivation":"from a compound of G1909 (ἐπί) and G2147 (εὑρίσκω);","strongs_def":" a discoverer, i.e. contriver","kjv_def":"inventor","n":1,"o":"ROM1:30"},"G2101":{"lemma":"εὐάρεστος","translit":"euárestos","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G701 (ἀρεστός);","strongs_def":" fully agreeable","kjv_def":"acceptable(-ted), wellpleasing","n":9,"o":"ROM12:1 ROM12:2 ROM14:18 2CO5:9 EPH5:10 PHP4:18 COL3:20 TIT2:9 HEB13:21"},"G2113":{"lemma":"εὐθυδρομέω","translit":"euthydroméō","derivation":"from G2117 (εὐθύς) and G1408 (δρόμος);","strongs_def":" to lay a straight course, i.e. sail direct","kjv_def":"(come) with a straight course","n":2,"o":"ACT16:11 ACT21:1"},"G2155":{"lemma":"εὔσπλαγχνος","translit":"eúsplanchnos","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G4698 (σπλάγχνον);","strongs_def":" well compassioned, i.e. sympathetic","kjv_def":"pitiful, tender-hearted","n":2,"o":"EPH4:32 1PE3:8"},"G2157":{"lemma":"εὐσχημοσύνη","translit":"euschēmosýnē","deriva