;","strongs_def":" good at imparting, i.e. liberal","kjv_def":"ready to distribute","n":1,"o":"1TI6:18"},"G2176":{"lemma":"εὐώνυμος","translit":"euṓnymos","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G3686 (ὄνομα);","strongs_def":" properly, well-named (good-omened), i.e. the left (which was the lucky side among the pagan Greeks); neuter as adverbial, at the left hand","kjv_def":"(on the) left","n":10,"o":"MAT20:21 MAT20:23 MAT25:33 MAT25:41 MAT27:38 MRK10:37 MRK10:40 MRK15:27 ACT21:3 REV10:2"},"G2149":{"lemma":"εὐρύχωρος","translit":"eurýchōros","derivation":"from (wide) and G5561 (χώρα);","strongs_def":" spacious","kjv_def":"broad","n":1,"o":"MAT7:13"},"G2180":{"lemma":"Ἐφέσιος","translit":"Ephésios","derivation":"from G2181 (Ἔφεσος);","strongs_def":" an Ephesian or inhabitant of Ephesus","kjv_def":"Ephesian, of Ephesus","n":4,"o":"ACT19:28 ACT19:34 ACT19:35 ACT21:29"},"G2136":{"lemma":"Εὐοδία","translit":"Euodía","derivation":"from the same as G2137 (εὐοδόω);","strongs_def":" fine travelling; Euodia, a Christian woman","kjv_def":"Euodias","n":1,"o":"PHP4:2"},"G2111":{"lemma":"εὔθετος","translit":"eúthetos","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and a derivative of G5087 (τίθημι);","strongs_def":" well placed, i.e. (figuratively) appropriate","kjv_def":"fit, meet","n":3,"o":"LUK9:62 LUK14:35 HEB6:7"},"G2129":{"lemma":"εὐλογία","translit":"eulogía","derivation":"from the same as G2127 (εὐλογέω);","strongs_def":" fine speaking, i.e. elegance of language; commendation (\"eulogy\"), i.e. (reverentially) adoration; religiously, benediction; by implication, consecration; by extension, benefit or largess","kjv_def":"blessing (a matter of) bounty (X -tifully), fair speech","n":14,"o":"ROM15:29 ROM16:18 1CO10:16 2CO9:5 2CO9:6 GAL3:14 EPH1:3 HEB6:7 HEB12:17 JAS3:10 1PE3:9 REV5:12 REV5:13 REV7:12"},"G2158":{"lemma":"εὐσχήμων","translit":"euschḗmōn","derivation":"from G2095 (εὖ) and G4976 (σχῆμα);","strongs_def":" well-formed, i.e. (figuratively) decorous, noble (in rank)","kjv_def":"comely, hon